# Patch 0008 — one writer per sidecar: withStoreLock, taken by track-edit, track-comment and track-reply
# Offered back: no (not yet: written as offerable to the engine's author, held back by the standing word of 2026-09-11 to open nothing new upstream)
# Files: store-io.mjs, cli/track-comment.mjs, cli/track-edit.mjs, cli/track-reply.mjs
#
# Reason: every writer of a sidecar loads it, changes the object and renames a temp over it, and
# two writers interleaved between load and rename each save a store that lacks the other's
# change, so the second rename erases the first's write (a reply lost under an editor host's
# comment, an edit's op lost under a reply). Measured against the real CLIs and an editor host,
# one write in five was lost at a stagger of 4 to 20 ms (2026-09-09); a stat before the rename
# narrows that window and cannot close it. store-io gains withStoreLock(storePath, fn): an O_EXCL
# create of `<sidecar>.lock` holding "pid ts", a few milliseconds' sleep and retry for up to
# STORE_LOCK_WAIT_MS (2 s) when held, a StoreLockError past that (held: true) or when the name is
# taken by a non-lock or cannot be created (held: false), a break of a lock whose writer is dead
# or whose stamp is older than STORE_LOCK_STALE_MS (15 s), the unlink in finally, and the
# `.trackchanges/` folder made for the lock when missing and removed again when nothing landed
# in it. The three CLIs take it around their load-to-rename (track-edit: the file read through
# the file write and the thread turn; track-comment and track-reply: the note read through the
# save), printing "another editor is writing this file; retry" and exiting 1 when it is not
# obtained. Their fail() now throws a CliFailure the entry point prints and exits 1 on, instead
# of exiting on the spot, so a lock held at that moment is released (process.exit skips every
# finally); the exit status and the message are unchanged. The exported pure functions keep
# their signatures. Tests: tools/vendor-patches.test.mjs (P8 cases) and
# tools/file-comments-host-store-lock.test.mjs (the CLIs waiting for a held lock).
